:{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":16,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The verdict for CAT-04 is **pass**, written to `tasks/CAT-04/judge.md`. I changed no code and ran no other stage.\n\nCAT-04 is an adopted story, so the only question was whether each of the 7 new tests proves its scenario. Each one sets up the Given, performs the When and checks every Then with the story's exact wording. Each of the 7 break patches changes exactly the thing its test checks. I checked that by reading them; I didn't apply them, and the gate report has no line showing they were run and turned red.\n\nThe test levels match the rules: one browser test for the happy path and six HTTP-level integration tests for the rest.\n\n**One minor finding, which doesn't block but needs you:** the browser test's title, \"Home page welcomes the visitor\", isn't a scenario in `dca-sample-specification/scenarios.md` yet.\n- **Effect:** the normal build and CI stay green. But a run with `-p:SpecificationPath=…` set would fail `SharedScenariosTest`, because it finds a test without a scenario.\n- **Fix:** you own the scenarios, so this is yours to add. It needs a scenario with that exact title in the specification, plus a Java test under the same title.\n\nThe review perspective carriers (`review-ddd`, `review-hexagonal`, `review-clean-code`, `dca-review`) didn't run: no production code changed. I didn't consult `dca-knowledge`, because no finding depended on a pattern question.","ttft_ms":4391,"type":"result","duration_ms":92070,"uuid":"f5af72db-cc0c-4e76-8d73-25f678b243d4","ttft_stream_ms":3387,"time_to_request_ms":45,"first_content_frame_ms":3387,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
